{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-04-09 12:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E CONTRIBUTES $500,000 TO RESTAURANT RESILIENCE FUND TO STRENGTHEN BUSINESSES FOR THE LONG-TERM', 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--BEGINNING NEXT WEEK, RESTAURANTS IN SIX NORTHERN AND CENTRAL CALIFORNIA COUNTIES CAN APPLY FOR A $3,500 GRANT TO HELP THEM REBOUND FROM THE ECONOMIC IMPACTS OF THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC. THE CALIFORNIA RESTAURANT FOUNDATION'S (CRF) RESTAURANTS CARE RESILIENCE FUND IS ACCEPTING APPLICATIONS APRIL 11-18, 2021. PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E) CONTRIBUTED $500,000 TO THE FUND TO ASSIST SMALL RESTAURANTS STRUGGLING IN THE WAKE OF STAY-AT-HOME ORDERS AND OTHER"}